A||||28||btoth||Nissan's 350Z||||6||
Z||000000||btoth||11-06-2001||06:41 PM||||Got my Road & Track in the mail today.  Has the first drive of the new 350Z.  I'm happy and disapointed at the same time.  Overall I'm glad that they stuck with RWD (just wouldn't be the same with FWD), and the interior looks simple and sporty, and it has enough power going for it (normally asperated too!).<P>What I would change are the funky door handles, and the tail lights.  I always thought the 90's Z had the coolest taillights - I wish they brought them back.  It's hard to tell by the picture if the new ones are really that bad though.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  I also think that the side of the car needs some molding or ground effects or something to break up the side a bit.  <P>Just my opinion.  What do think??||||reg||6
Z||000001||btoth||11-07-2001||11:22 AM|||| <A HREF="http://www.roadandtrack.com/RoadAndTrack/features/bts/1201_bts_nissan_350z_p1.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.roadandtrack.com/RoadAndTrack/features/bts/1201_bts_nissan_350z_p1.html</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||falconhulk||11-07-2001||11:51 AM||||"With a curb weight somewhere in the neighborhood of 3150 lb. and 280 bhp on tap, the 350Z should see 60 mph in about 6.0 seconds and the quarter mile in 14.0 seconds."???????  That  sux.  Thats not even as good as the fbodies.  I thought they were going to go for corvette numbers.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||frontal lobe||11-07-2001||12:08 PM||||I guess the looks are ok, not awesome.<P>Sad when you are sitting there thinking, "Hmmm, should I get this or the Altima, get about the same engine and 2 more doors", instead of thinking should I get this or a corvette?!?!||||reg||1
Z||000004||FLASHY||11-07-2001||01:28 PM||||I think it looks nice.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/nissanZ1.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/nissanZ2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Brandon86SE||11-07-2001||01:32 PM||||I have to agree with Flashy, I think it looks good.  Plus, I'm not aware of any Altima's that put out 280hp, or look that good.  I actually think it looks an awful lot like the Charger R/T concept released a couple years ago.||||reg||1
Z||000006||falconhulk||11-07-2001||01:39 PM||||Yes it looks like a concept.  Not something that makes it to the road.  Ther performance numbers just dont make sense for a 30k sports car.  I could understand if it was 30k for convertable and like 24k for the loaded standard.  It would have been great if it was released 6 years ago.  Its looks make it stand out but its kind of like the Fiero in that way.  It will turn heads but you will always be challanged by faster cars because of its looks.  14.0 is not slow by any means.  Just a little off what they claimed from the start.  They claimed corvette performance at a more affordable price.  The price is more afforable but the vette will still blow it away.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Nashco||11-07-2001||01:56 PM||||I saw this car at the Detroit Auto Show last year, and at first I didn't believe they'd be putting that thing to production.  It was just TOO cool, and quick to boot.  Well, as time progresses, it sounds more and more likely to hit shelves soon!  Personally, I love the look.  I think the Z cars rock..from any era; some weren't that great stock, but they all have serious potential.  A coworker has a 240z that he's turboed and done tons of suspension, wheel, brake, interior, etc. work to.  That car looks like it's straight out of a James Bond movie!<P>Also, I don't think the cost is too high for what you get.  You're getting great 1/4 mile times, but not as good as some American grunt, true.  BUT, how well will it corner and brake in comparison?  How much more comfortable will it be?  How much better will it hold up in comparison?  How much quieter, smoother, and sturdy is it?  What kind of quality can you expect compared to an American car...especially in the interior and drivetrain components?  I'm almost willing to bet the new Z would top most American cars in those categories...not too much competition in some of those areas.<P>I would like the new RX-8 to come out as well, and I think it will.  It is a great competitor for the new Z, and the demand is out there.  The RX-7 model discontinued as the Fiero...it was at it's prime when they cut it's throat!  The last RX-7 model brings a pretty penny in the used car business....they have hardly depreciated!  It has some very nice features, as well, and I welcome both of these cars to the market...more eye candy <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000008||frontal lobe||11-07-2001||03:18 PM||||Altima has the 3.5 in it, but with reported 240 h.p.  Maxima version of the 3.5 is 260 h.p., I think.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Berserk||11-07-2001||03:23 PM||||How much you want to bet there'll be a turbo version in a year or two?||||reg||1
Z||000010||btoth||11-07-2001||03:32 PM||||It comes out next summer as a 2003 model.  This is the same engine used in the Maxima but with better intake and exhaust.  Just like the '90s 300zx (they used the Maxima SE engine with the dual overhead cams).  <P>Multilink suspension on all four corners.<P>They say that their target was Porsche Boxters and cars like that.<P>The '90s 300zx convertables were very rare when they were made, and still sell for outrageous prices.  The local dealership has one for $24000.  It would be great if the prices on those came down when the new ones come out.||||reg||1
Z||000011||btoth||11-07-2001||03:36 PM||||According to R&T:  2001 Maxima = 222bhp/217lb-ft. of torque.||||reg||1
Z||000012||Monkeyman||11-07-2001||03:43 PM||||Personally, I think it's ugly.  Especially the headlights and grille.  That doesn't look like a very original concept.  Just another clone.||||reg||1
